# ─── Frontend Environment Variables (PM2 / Production) ────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to frontend/.env before running `npm run build`.
# VITE_ variables are baked into the JS bundle at build time by Vite.
# Changing them requires a rebuild + PM2 restart.
#
# ── How API URL is resolved (no .env needed for basic PM2 deploy) ──────────────
#
# The app auto-detects the backend URL at runtime:
#
#  Local dev  (localhost)  →  http://localhost:5001
#  PM2 deploy (same server) →  http://<server-ip>:5001   ← auto-detected
#  Custom domain / Nginx   →  set VITE_API_URL below
#
# ── Set VITE_API_URL only if: ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  1. You use Nginx to proxy /api on the same domain (no port in URL):
#       VITE_API_URL=https://yourdomain.com
#
#  2. Backend is on a completely different domain:
#       VITE_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
#
#  3. You want to override the auto-detected port for any reason:
#       VITE_API_URL=http://YOUR_SERVER_IP:5001
#
# For a plain PM2 deploy on the same server, you can leave this UNSET.
# VITE_API_URL=
